ion.json"} {"question" "q-98700" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/state.json" "file_sha256" "fa65cf2bcabbbca651d41e227125b822e2d9285cef23bb30e73d812fcb66a6c1" "basis" 1585 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-339664" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/assets/528bf1bc9d6177f031b8b5504641903a11dfc2c2576e4759bf4cb7c278d0585c.png)\n\nA particular autonomous differential equation has the phase line shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $y=0$ is a sink\n- $y=3$ is a source\n- $y=3$ is a node" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/state.json" "file_sha256" "fa65cf2bcabbbca651d41e227125b822e2d9285cef23bb30e73d812fcb66a6c1" "basis" 1585 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-339664" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can classify the equilibrium solutions of an autonomous ODE ${y}^{′}=f(y)$ by examining its phase line.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *sink* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *toward* the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *source* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *away* from the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *node* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line point in the same direction.\n\nLet's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true. Notice that the arrow just above the point $y=0$ points downward, and the arrow just below it points upward. In other words, both arrows point *toward* the point $y=0.$ This means that $y=0$ is a sink.\n\n- Statement II is true, while statement III is false. Notice that the arrow just above the point $y=3$ points upward, and the arrow just below it points downward. In other words, both arrows point *away* from $y=3.$ This means that $y=3$ is a source.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/state.json" "file_sha256" "fa65cf2bcabbbca651d41e227125b822e2d9285cef23bb30e73d812fcb66a6c1" "basis" 1585 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-339664" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cd657abdb9731a4425d0f9e1d47f2819274d21f473ed4ef4aec657eea27e5372" "basis" 1585 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-339664" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/state.json" "file_sha256" "fa65cf2bcabbbca651d41e227125b822e2d9285cef23bb30e73d812fcb66a6c1" "basis" 1585 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-339664" "f