ion/problem" "value" "Which of the following statements is true regarding the equilibrium solutions of ${y}^{′}={y}^{2}+6y+9?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/state.json" "file_sha256" "fa65cf2bcabbbca651d41e227125b822e2d9285cef23bb30e73d812fcb66a6c1" "basis" 1585 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-98763" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can classify the equilibrium solutions of an autonomous ODE ${y}^{′}=f(y)$ by examining its phase line.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *sink* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *toward* the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *source* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *away* from the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *node* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line point in the same direction.\n\nFirst, we need to find the equilibrium solutions. So, we solve $f(y)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(y) & =0 \\\\ {y}^{2}+6y+9 & =0 \\\\ (y+3)^{2} & =0 \\\\ y & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equilibrium solution is $y=-3.$ \n\nNow, we analyze the sign of $f(y)$ using a sign table, as follows:\n\n|  | $(-\\infty ,-3)$ | $(3,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $(y+3)^{2}$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $f(y)$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n\nSo, we have that $f(y)$ is positive for $y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nWe can now draw the phase line for this equation.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/assets/074ed04c41f20a891678d61a26ae06f1151299110dfd13d2c8b7f6eef3e6e363.png)\n\nFinally, we classify the equilibrium solution:\n\n- $y=-3$ is a node because it is neither a source nor a sink.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$y=-3$ is a node\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/state.json" "file_sha256" "fa65cf2bcabbbca651d41e227125b822e2d9285cef23bb30e73d812fcb66a6c1" "basis" 1585 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-98763" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cd657abdb9731a4425d0f9e1d47f2819274d21f473ed4ef4aec657eea27e5372" "basis" 1585 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-98763" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/state.json" "file_sha256" "fa65cf2bcabbbca651d41e227125b822e2d9285cef23bb30e73d812fcb66a6c1" "basis" 1585 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-98763" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "$y=-3$ is a node"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/state.json" "file_sha256" "fa65cf2bcabbbca651d41e227125b822e2d9285cef23bb30e73d812fcb66a6c1" "basis" 1585 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-98763" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "$y=-3$ is a node and $y=3$ is a sink"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/state.json" "file_sha256" "fa65cf2bcabbbca651d41e227125b822e2d9285cef23bb30e73d812fcb66a6c1" "basis" 1585 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-98763" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "$y=-3$ is a node and $y=3$ is a source"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/state.json" "file_sha256" "fa65cf2bcabbbca651d41e227125b822e2d9285cef23bb30e73d812fcb66a6c1" "basis" 1585 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-98763" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "$y=-3$ is a sink"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/state.json" "file_sha256" "fa65cf2bcabbbca651d41e227125b822e2d9285cef23bb30e73d812fcb66a6c1" "basis" 1585 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-98763" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "$y=-3$ is a source"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/state.json" "file_sha256" "fa65cf2bcabbbca651d41e227125b822e2d9285cef23bb30e73d812fcb66a6c1" "basis" 1585 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-98763" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$y=-3$ is a node"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/state.json" "file_sha256" "fa65cf2bcabbbca651d41e227125b822e2d9285cef23bb30e73d812fcb66a6c1" "basis" 1585 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-98760" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following statements is true regarding the equilibrium solutions of ${y}^{′}=-(y-3)({y}^{2}+6y+9)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/state.json" "file_sha256" "fa65cf2bcabbbca651d41e227125b822e2d9285cef23bb30e73d812fcb66a6c1" "basis" 1585 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-98760" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can classify the equilibrium solutions of an autonomous ODE ${y}^{′}=f(y)$ by examining its phase line.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *sink* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *toward* the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *source* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *away* from the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *node* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line point in the same direction.\n\nFirst, we need to find the equilibrium solutions. So, we solve $f(y)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(y) & =0 \\\\ -(y-3)({y}^{2}+6y+9) & =0 \\\\ -(y-3)(y+3)^{2} & =0 \\\\ y & =-3,3,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equilibrium solutions are $y=-3$ and $y=3.$\n\nNow, we analyze the sign of $f(y)$ using a sign table, as follows:\n\n|  | $(-\\infty ,-3)$ | $(-3,3)$ | $(3,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-(y-3)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| $(y+3)^{2}$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $f(y)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n\nSo, we have that $f(y)$ is positive for $y\\in (-\\infty ,3),$ and negative for $y\\in (3,\\infty ).$\n\nWe can now draw the phase line for this equation.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/assets/3c118c900486d8561864c88e1b25a461c8f459f810bb7b753d30d9d0d4780913.png)\n\nFinally, we classify the equilibrium solutions:\n\n- $y=-3$  is a node because it is neither a source nor a sink.\n\n- $y=3$ is a sink because the nearby solutions converge toward this point.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$y=-3$ is a node, and $y=3$ is a sink\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/state.json" "file_sha256" "fa65cf2bcabbbca651d41e227125b822e2d9285cef23bb30e73d812fcb66a6c1" "basis" 1585 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-98760" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cd657abdb9731a4425d0f9e1d47f2819274d21f473ed4ef4aec657eea27e5372" "basis" 1585 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-98760" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/math