.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *node* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line point in the same direction.\n\nFirst, we draw the phase line with the given information. \n\nNote that there are $2$ equilibrium points, $y=-3$ and $y=2.$\n\n- We're given that $y=-3$ is a source. We represent this on the phase line by drawing an upward-pointing arrow just above $y=-3$ and a downward-pointing arrow just below it.\n\n- We're given that $y=2$ is a node. This means that the arrows on either side of $y=2$ point in the same direction. Since the arrow just below $y=2$ points upward, the arrow just above it points upward too.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071359/assets/d03ab1d15be3656787d7ccd0114b2011f561bfed9c67d22f3366f50ed2f410e4.png)\n\nOf the given options, the only slope field that correspond with this phase line is the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071359/assets/890c699885c8694597912bd65044fde50dd99ac8757578dc0db71bdb413b5db7.png)\n\nNote that:\n\n- The slope field is horizontal at $y=-3$ and $y=2.$\n\n- The slopes near $y=-3$ appear to diverge away from this line.\n\n- The slopes near $y=2$ appear to diverge away from this line when we're looking above the line and appear to converge toward the line when we're looking below the line." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071359/state.json" "file_sha256" "83068dd279f9700418ab112c81f1a154e905bf991fa628cbdb13bc365339a79b"} {"question" "q-98790" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071359/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "efe3194dee45cd632f12dbb8b74a7e7c91cc152570ce123c26a02a83fbbf630a"} {"question" "q-98790" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/